1
00:04:07,058 --> 00:04:13,058
The Boomerang is a drama film directed by Bertram Bracken.

2
00:08:14,117 --> 00:08:20,117
Millionaire meat packer Peter Cameron, greedy for more money and power, maneuvers an alliance between his daughter Rose and
George Gray, the son of Cameron's business rival Max Gray, in order to increase his control of the food industry.

3
00:12:21,176 --> 00:12:27,176
George, a lawyer, opposes the trust, and as a result is professionally ruined by
Cameron, disinherited by his father, and jilted by his fiancée.

4
00:16:28,235 --> 00:16:34,235
Out on his own, George gets a job at a mill and starts at the bottom.

5
00:20:35,294 --> 00:20:41,294
When an epidemic breaks out among his fellow laborers due to their eating spoiled meat from the trust, George secures
evidence of criminal practices which ultimately brings about the conviction of Cameron and the trust.

6
00:24:42,352 --> 00:24:48,352
In championing the rights of the downtrodden, George
wins back Rose and reforms Cameron.

7
00:28:49,411 --> 00:28:55,411
George Gray, played by Henry B. Walthall.

8
00:32:56,470 --> 00:33:02,470
Peter Cameron, played by Melbourne MacDowell.

9
00:37:03,529 --> 00:37:09,529
Rose Cameron, played by Nina Byron.

